## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vite + React + TypeScript project.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.1.2)
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` with the new dependency

**2. Code Integration**
Modified `src/App.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the App component's return statement (after the Routes component)

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I:
1. Fetched the latest installation instructions from Vercel's documentation
2. Identified that this project uses Vite + React, requiring the React-specific implementation
3. Used the project's package manager (npm) to install the analytics package
4. Integrated the Analytics component at the root level of the application

The Analytics component is now placed in the main App component, ensuring it tracks page views across all routes including:
- Home page (/)
- Impressum page (/impressum)
- Privacy page (/privacy)

### Testing & Verification

✅ Build completed successfully - `npm run build` passed without errors
✅ Linter passed - `npm run lint` completed with no errors
✅ All dependencies properly installed and lock files updated

### Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project's Analytics section
   - Click the "Enable" button
3. After deployment, analytics data will start appearing in your Vercel dashboard

### Files Modified

- `dj-website-frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `dj-website-frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package installation
- `dj-website-frontend/src/App.tsx` - Imported and added Analytics component
